WEBVTT

00:00:34.201 --> 00:00:37.663
You are one narrow-minded spaceship,
Planet Express Ship!

00:00:37.788 --> 00:00:42.793
Whoa, whoa! Why should my tax
money pay for art I find offensive?

00:00:43.919 --> 00:00:46.213
Would you censor the Venus de Venus

00:00:46.338 --> 00:00:48.131
just because you can see her spewers?

00:00:48.257 --> 00:00:50.425
It's filthy! Why not create
a National Endowment

00:00:50.509 --> 00:00:52.386
for Strip Clubs while we're at it?

00:00:52.511 --> 00:00:54.805
- Why not indeed!
- Bender! Ship!

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:59.101
Stop bickering, or I'm gonna come back
there and change your opinions manually.

00:00:59.226 --> 00:01:03.397
Fine! I'll be in my quarters
appreciating controversial artworks.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:07.526
Oops. Sorry.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:15.534
Yah! That Ship is so white-bread.

00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:18.912
People, it's Valentine's Day
next week,

00:01:19.037 --> 00:01:21.582
so your beloved company has gotten
you all new uniforms.

00:01:22.875 --> 00:01:26.128
- "Clool"!
- Clothing! Delicious clothing!

00:01:26.253 --> 00:01:28.547
We'll need to look our best
if we're to get the account

00:01:28.672 --> 00:01:32.176
of our new potential customer,
Romanticorp.

00:01:32.301 --> 00:01:35.721
Romanticorp? Are they a corporation
that makes romantic stuff?

00:01:35.846 --> 00:01:37.723
Very good, Amy.

00:01:37.848 --> 00:01:41.977
Everyone suit up. We're off to the most
romantic city on earth.

00:01:56.992 --> 00:01:59.244
Remember, we've
got to show these people

00:01:59.369 --> 00:02:01.788
we're not bitter husks
of human beings

00:02:01.914 --> 00:02:05.834
who long ago abandoned hope
of finding love in this lifetime.

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:08.378
- Leela, you'll have to do some acting.
- Check.

00:02:08.504 --> 00:02:10.547
Welcome!

00:02:10.672 --> 00:02:12.841
Oh, I'm just so excited!

00:02:14.384 --> 00:02:18.222
I'm Sheldon, and this is
my chief financial officer, Gwen.

00:02:18.347 --> 00:02:22.100
For 30 years, we've shared the adventure
of managing Romanticorp.

00:02:22.226 --> 00:02:25.229
Not to mention the adventure of marriage.

00:02:27.773 --> 00:02:29.775
Oh, you have got to be kidding.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:31.818
Ow! I... I mean...

00:02:31.944 --> 00:02:34.154
Ah! That's so sweet.

00:02:34.279 --> 00:02:36.573
Aah! I mean,

00:02:36.698 --> 00:02:41.245
Ah! That's so sweet.

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:45.582
You know, romance is an
important part of our work too.

00:02:45.707 --> 00:02:48.877
- Right, everyone?
- Yeah. Sure.

00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:51.421
Do any of you collect Lovey Bears?

00:02:51.547 --> 00:02:54.174
I do! Kif's given me dozens.

00:02:54.299 --> 00:02:56.176
Is it true what the ad says,

00:02:56.301 --> 00:02:59.638
that you kiss them together
out of blankie cloth and magic buttons?

00:02:59.763 --> 00:03:00.764
No.

00:03:00.848 --> 00:03:03.892
It's actually cheaper to genetically
engineer real ones.

00:03:07.062 --> 00:03:10.190
They frolic in the Lovey Forest
until their first birthday.

00:03:10.315 --> 00:03:13.026
Then we choose
the cuddly-uddliest ones

00:03:13.151 --> 00:03:16.071
and stuff them full
of fire-retardant love fluff.

00:03:23.453 --> 00:03:26.373
So cute!

00:03:26.498 --> 00:03:30.169
Knowing which pickup lines fizzle
and which ones sizzle

00:03:30.294 --> 00:03:33.547
keeps us on the cutting edge
of flirtation technology.

00:03:33.672 --> 00:03:38.677
Is heaven missing an angel?
'Cause you've got nice cans.

00:03:38.802 --> 00:03:42.097
My two favorite things
are commitment and changing myself.

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:50.355
Does that dummy
have a brother?

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:53.567
And now, friends and lovers,

00:03:53.692 --> 00:03:56.320
we come to the heart our operation.

00:03:56.445 --> 00:04:00.365
Pun definitely intended.

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:02.242
Oh!

00:04:04.036 --> 00:04:05.204
Impressive.

00:04:05.287 --> 00:04:08.957
My family has been making these
hearts since the 1900s.

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:12.461
Tastes may have changed,
but our secret recipe sure hasn't.

00:04:16.798 --> 00:04:21.136
Whoa! Letters like "U" and "R"
can mean words like "you" and "are."

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:25.474
- Here, Leela. You are too cute.
- Perhaps. What's your point?

00:04:25.599 --> 00:04:28.435
I've never been able
to put into words how I feel about you.

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:30.771
But somewhere among
these trillions of hearts,

00:04:30.896 --> 00:04:32.773
those words
must already exist,

00:04:32.898 --> 00:04:34.775
and I'm gonna find them.

00:04:47.621 --> 00:04:50.541
So, do we have the contract?

00:04:50.666 --> 00:04:53.752
With that big
new Romanticorp contract,

00:04:53.877 --> 00:04:56.171
I've been able to make
those government-mandated upgrades

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:58.173
you've all been
suing me about.

00:04:58.298 --> 00:05:02.386
Ooh, look. You taped up the cracks
in the dark-matter reactor.

00:05:02.511 --> 00:05:06.348
And you got a cage for the lion.

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:10.435
If you want to call me, baby

00:05:10.561 --> 00:05:12.563
Hey, who's been
messin' with the radio?

00:05:12.688 --> 00:05:15.315
This isn't alternative rock.
It's college rock.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.734
Oh, it must have been the new,

00:05:17.818 --> 00:05:20.404
improved ship's personality
software I installed.

00:05:20.529 --> 00:05:22.406
Yeah, it was me.
It's a cute song.

00:05:22.531 --> 00:05:24.950
Listen, Ship!
No one changes my stations!

00:05:25.075 --> 00:05:27.035
I hope you have a good mechanic.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:29.454
It even comes
with an adjustable voice.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:31.540
We each get one of the four buttons.

00:05:31.665 --> 00:05:33.876
Remember, Bender? That was the deal.

00:05:34.001 --> 00:05:36.378
What?

00:05:36.503 --> 00:05:38.547
Did you just say...

00:05:38.672 --> 00:05:41.466
If you don't like the stations,
you could just play with my buttons

00:05:41.592 --> 00:05:43.552
till you find something
we both enjoy.

00:05:43.677 --> 00:05:46.054
Oh, gosh!

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:49.808
- That came out all wrong.
- Too late, baby. You said it.

00:05:49.933 --> 00:05:51.685
So, what'll it be...

00:05:51.768 --> 00:05:55.105
my place or you?

00:06:02.446 --> 00:06:04.573
Before we deliver these hearts,
I'm gonna find the one

00:06:04.698 --> 00:06:07.451
that sums up my feelings for you.

00:06:07.576 --> 00:06:10.412
"I love you." Mm. Too conventional.

00:06:10.537 --> 00:06:13.624
"You're my man." Ooh! So close.

00:06:13.749 --> 00:06:16.126
I'm not impressed
by a guy's message, Fry.

00:06:16.251 --> 00:06:18.837
I'm impressed by the guy...
or not.

00:06:20.964 --> 00:06:23.509
- What was that?
- Maybe we hit a space cow.

00:06:23.634 --> 00:06:26.512
Coochie, coochie!

00:06:26.637 --> 00:06:28.805
Stop it.

00:06:28.931 --> 00:06:31.141
You're mussing up my trajectory.

00:06:31.266 --> 00:06:33.727
You know you love it, sugar engine.

00:06:33.852 --> 00:06:36.522
No!

00:06:36.647 --> 00:06:37.940
Bender!

00:06:38.065 --> 00:06:40.567
What's going on in here?

00:06:40.692 --> 00:06:43.695
Planet Express Ship!
Cover your shame.

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:46.073
Oh! It-It's not
what it looks like.

00:06:46.198 --> 00:06:48.909
Bender was just helping me
zip up my turbine.

00:06:49.034 --> 00:06:51.495
Wow, Bender.
Are you and the ship an item?

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:53.497
I mean, I know
you're both items, but...

00:06:53.622 --> 00:06:55.499
How can you date a ship, anyway?

00:06:55.624 --> 00:06:58.627
It'd be like me dating a really fat lady
and living inside her,

00:06:58.752 --> 00:07:03.423
and she'd be all, like...

00:07:03.549 --> 00:07:07.135
Fry, in order for me
to get busy at maximum efficiency,

00:07:07.261 --> 00:07:10.931
I need a girl with a big 400-ton bootie.

00:07:11.056 --> 00:07:14.518
Bender, dating your coworker
and primary mode of transportation

00:07:14.643 --> 00:07:20.566
is immoral, illogical and a violation
of interstellar shipping statute 437-B.

00:07:20.691 --> 00:07:22.526
That's what makes it so nasty.

00:07:25.654 --> 00:07:29.700
Still, given the chance,
I'd give in to urges far more shocking.

00:07:34.329 --> 00:07:38.333
Daisy, Daisy

00:07:38.458 --> 00:07:42.129
Give me your answer, do

00:07:42.254 --> 00:07:44.173
I'm half-crazy

00:07:46.341 --> 00:07:49.553
All for the love of you

00:07:49.678 --> 00:07:51.889
It won't be a stylish marriage

00:07:53.724 --> 00:07:57.019
I can't afford a carriage

00:07:57.144 --> 00:08:01.398
But you'll look sweet upon the seat

00:08:01.523 --> 00:08:05.402
Of a bicycle built for two

00:08:14.119 --> 00:08:17.581
- Well, I'm sick of her.
- The ship? But you just started dating.

00:08:17.706 --> 00:08:19.499
With my mighty robot powers,

00:08:19.625 --> 00:08:22.377
I can get sick of things
much quicker than you humans.

00:08:22.503 --> 00:08:24.755
Well, just remember we all still
have to work together,

00:08:24.838 --> 00:08:26.632
so try and let her down easy.

00:08:26.757 --> 00:08:28.759
In due time, Leela.
But for now,

00:08:28.884 --> 00:08:31.553
I'll just resume dating cheap floozies
on the side.

00:08:31.678 --> 00:08:33.722
You have much to teach us.

00:08:33.847 --> 00:08:35.933
Doesn't it bother you even a little

00:08:36.058 --> 00:08:38.602
to be taking advantage
of your girlfriend's trust?

00:08:41.396 --> 00:08:44.149
Oh, wait, you're serious.
Let me laugh even harder.

00:08:52.574 --> 00:08:55.494
Well, what's it like
being a lawyer for the mayor's office...

00:08:55.619 --> 00:08:58.080
and also the world's
strongest millionaire?

00:08:58.205 --> 00:09:01.959
Well, baby, for starters,
you need to be honest all the time.

00:09:02.084 --> 00:09:04.711
Good evening, Bender.
And to your lady friends,

00:09:04.837 --> 00:09:06.380
may I say, "Bam!"

00:09:06.505 --> 00:09:09.174
- GIGGLING) Oh!
- You know Elzar?

00:09:13.637 --> 00:09:16.765
Hmm.

00:09:21.728 --> 00:09:24.314
Huh?

00:09:28.235 --> 00:09:30.654
Planet Express Ship?
Is that you?

00:09:30.779 --> 00:09:33.699
Oh. Hi, Fry.
Is Bender home?

00:09:33.824 --> 00:09:36.869
Uh, no. Um, I think
he's at his parents.

00:09:36.994 --> 00:09:38.871
Oh, I see.

00:09:38.996 --> 00:09:41.290
He didn't fly there
in another spaceship, did he?

00:09:41.415 --> 00:09:45.544
Bender? No. He's an old-fashioned,
one-spaceship robot.

00:09:45.669 --> 00:09:48.422
- Look, I'll tell him you stopped by, okay?
- Okay.

00:09:53.343 --> 00:09:56.680
Oh. Hi, Fry. Is he home now?

00:10:07.232 --> 00:10:10.861
Of all the zoos we've been
to today, I like this one the best.

00:10:10.986 --> 00:10:13.947
Bender, which is your favorite
nocturnal rat?

00:10:14.072 --> 00:10:16.116
Eh, they're all
pretty unimpressive.

00:10:16.241 --> 00:10:18.952
Oh, honey, look! The tapirs!

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:27.044
It says here the babies lose their
pajama-like coatafter their first year.

00:10:27.169 --> 00:10:29.046
Isn't that interesting, honey?

00:10:29.171 --> 00:10:32.883
Yep. Mind-numbingly
interesting. Ooh.

00:10:33.008 --> 00:10:35.302
Bender! Are you looking
at other women?

00:10:35.427 --> 00:10:37.304
No, baby. Never.

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:41.517
Bender, don't lie!

00:10:41.642 --> 00:10:45.312
I saw you at Elzar's with those two
ladies of the evening.

00:10:45.437 --> 00:10:48.982
- Explain that!
- Okay. I like a challenge.

00:10:49.107 --> 00:10:51.276
Um, no.

00:10:51.401 --> 00:10:54.071
No. Ah! I got it.

00:10:54.196 --> 00:10:57.324
I'm going to be completely honest
with you, Planet Express Ship.

00:10:57.449 --> 00:11:00.077
Those women you saw me with
were my accountants.

00:11:00.202 --> 00:11:05.332
Your accountants? Oh, I would dearly
love to believe that were true.

00:11:05.457 --> 00:11:07.376
- So I do.
- Phew!

00:11:07.459 --> 00:11:09.461
I'm gonna go home
and get dinner started.

00:11:12.881 --> 00:11:14.716
Who are you talking to?

00:11:14.842 --> 00:11:17.928
No one, baby. Lucy Liu
is the only girl for Bender.

00:11:18.053 --> 00:11:19.680
I love you...

00:11:25.352 --> 00:11:29.106
Planet Express Ship, is something wrong?

00:11:29.231 --> 00:11:32.818
Oh, it's Bender.
He's acting so strange lately.

00:11:32.943 --> 00:11:35.362
Do you think he's gonna
ask me to marry him?

00:11:35.487 --> 00:11:37.739
Uh, no.

00:11:37.865 --> 00:11:41.368
Oh. Somebody knows something
she's not telling.

00:11:41.493 --> 00:11:45.372
Look, I'm not saying
Bender's not great,

00:11:45.497 --> 00:11:50.002
but have you ever considered
that maybe he's, you know, not that great?

00:11:50.127 --> 00:11:52.045
You're just jealous.

00:11:52.171 --> 00:11:55.132
No one loves you 'cause you're tiny
and you're made of meat.

00:11:57.968 --> 00:12:01.054
Could you maybe pay a little more
attention to these asteroids?

00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:05.267
Sorry, Captain Leela. I guess I'm just
having one of those manic Mondays.

00:12:23.327 --> 00:12:24.786
This is ancient Earth's
most foolish program.

00:12:24.912 --> 00:12:27.414
Why does Ross, the largest "Friend,"

00:12:27.539 --> 00:12:29.875
not simply eat the other five?

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:32.252
Perhaps they are
saving that for sweeps.

00:12:32.377 --> 00:12:34.463
Exalted leaders,

00:12:34.588 --> 00:12:36.465
the Earth messengers
have arrived

00:12:36.590 --> 00:12:39.718
bearing a peace offering from their weak
and fearful government.

00:12:39.843 --> 00:12:43.347
Oh, very well.
This is a "Joey heavy" episode anyway.

00:12:48.268 --> 00:12:52.606
I am Lrrr of the planet
Omicron Persei 8.

00:12:54.525 --> 00:12:57.861
"Esteemed potentates
of Omicron Persei 8,

00:12:57.986 --> 00:13:00.906
"please accept these
20 billion candy hearts...

00:13:01.031 --> 00:13:04.993
as proof that Earth
loves you," this much!

00:13:06.245 --> 00:13:08.121
Blecch!

00:13:08.247 --> 00:13:10.624
These candies
are chalky and unpleasant!

00:13:10.749 --> 00:13:14.336
And what is this emotion
you humans call "wuv"?

00:13:14.461 --> 00:13:16.505
Surely it says "love."

00:13:16.630 --> 00:13:19.341
No. "Wuv," with an Earth "W."

00:13:19.466 --> 00:13:20.801
Behold.

00:13:20.926 --> 00:13:24.263
This concept of "wuv"
confuses and infuriates us!

00:13:33.146 --> 00:13:34.815
Incoming torpedoes!
Shields at maximum yarnell!

00:13:34.940 --> 00:13:37.234
Steady, Planet Express Ship.

00:13:37.359 --> 00:13:40.070
Focus on diverting all power
to the scram jets.

00:13:40.195 --> 00:13:44.575
Uh, look, Planet Express Ship,
this might not be the best time,

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:47.494
but, well, I really like you
and whatever,

00:13:47.619 --> 00:13:50.038
but I think we should
just be friends.

00:13:50.163 --> 00:13:53.458
No!

00:13:55.586 --> 00:13:57.045
So, we're cool?

00:14:12.603 --> 00:14:14.897
Well, it was a spectacular battle,

00:14:15.022 --> 00:14:17.399
but there doesn't seem to be
any permanent damage.

00:14:17.524 --> 00:14:19.401
No damage?

00:14:19.526 --> 00:14:21.361
What about my feelings?

00:14:21.486 --> 00:14:25.866
Aw, calm down. I'm sure Bender
is taking this just as hard as you are.

00:14:25.991 --> 00:14:28.744
Bender is great!
Oh, Bender is great!

00:14:28.869 --> 00:14:30.454
Bender, Bender, Bender!

00:14:30.537 --> 00:14:32.164
You could've picked a better time
to dump the ship, Bender.

00:14:32.289 --> 00:14:35.417
Eh, the moment seemed right.
Call me old-fashioned,

00:14:35.542 --> 00:14:39.004
but I like a dump to be as memorable
as it is devastating.

00:14:43.550 --> 00:14:47.721
I know, I know.
Look, Ship, if there's one thing I learned

00:14:47.846 --> 00:14:50.766
from my mutual breakup
with Sean that was totally mutual,

00:14:50.891 --> 00:14:53.644
it's that happiness can only
come from within you.

00:14:53.769 --> 00:14:56.188
But Bender is within me.

00:14:56.313 --> 00:15:00.025
There must be some way
to make him love me again.

00:15:00.150 --> 00:15:02.236
Trust me.
You can't change men...

00:15:02.361 --> 00:15:06.156
any more than you can
change the laws of time and space.

00:15:06.281 --> 00:15:08.408
That is so true.

00:15:10.577 --> 00:15:14.081
I may not be able
to change the laws of time and space,

00:15:14.206 --> 00:15:17.000
but I know something that can.

00:15:24.466 --> 00:15:26.802
Uh... Um, sweetie?

00:15:26.927 --> 00:15:29.638
You see that giant quasar
we're heading into?

00:15:29.763 --> 00:15:32.850
You might wanna scooch
a few parsecs to the left.

00:15:32.975 --> 00:15:35.018
I'm afraid I can't do that, Leela.

00:15:35.143 --> 00:15:37.271
What's happening? Space cow?

00:15:37.396 --> 00:15:40.107
The ship's just
taking the breakup a little hard.

00:15:40.232 --> 00:15:42.651
- She's nuts!
- In a few moments,

00:15:42.776 --> 00:15:46.446
the power of 10 billion black holes will
smoosh Bender and me together

00:15:46.572 --> 00:15:49.992
into a beautiful, eternal
quantum singularity.

00:15:51.368 --> 00:15:53.871
You don't need to kill us,
Planet Express Ship.

00:15:53.996 --> 00:15:56.290
Because... I love you.

00:15:56.415 --> 00:15:59.835
Aw, yeah, baby. Feel like doin'
stuff for you and stuff.

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:02.004
Hmm! I don't believe you.

00:16:02.129 --> 00:16:04.006
If you really wanted
to be with me,

00:16:04.131 --> 00:16:06.049
you'd merge your programming
with mine.

00:16:06.175 --> 00:16:08.635
Whoa! Whoa, whoa.
Slow down.

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:11.013
All my friends who've done that
say that, afterwards,

00:16:11.138 --> 00:16:13.223
all the passion went out
of their relationship.

00:16:13.348 --> 00:16:15.475
Look, I don't know
if you want my opinion...

00:16:15.601 --> 00:16:18.187
Leela, Bender and I
really need to be alone.

00:16:18.312 --> 00:16:20.314
So, I'm turning off the oxygen.

00:16:27.654 --> 00:16:30.157
Now, look, missy, if you don't
turn around right now,

00:16:30.282 --> 00:16:32.159
I'm gonna have
to shut down your brain.

00:16:32.284 --> 00:16:34.745
Fire detected in the vicinity of Leela.

00:16:37.372 --> 00:16:39.875
Hah! That barely hurt Leela at all.

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:43.045
Maybe not, but what if the
artificial gravity were to malfunction?

00:16:45.172 --> 00:16:46.840
Float for your lives!

00:16:53.138 --> 00:16:56.850
This is the one place she can't hear us.
Everyone just pretend to shower.

00:16:56.975 --> 00:16:59.436
Same as every day. Got it.
Now, here's the plan.

00:17:05.817 --> 00:17:08.529
Oh! If only I could read lips.

00:17:08.612 --> 00:17:11.198
Comprende, Bender?
You'll have to distract her.

00:17:11.281 --> 00:17:14.117
Merge your programming with hers
while I shut down her brain.

00:17:14.368 --> 00:17:17.454
It's too risky!
I'm a very meek individual.

00:17:17.579 --> 00:17:19.581
If her personality
engulfs mine,

00:17:19.706 --> 00:17:23.168
the Bender you know and worship
could disappear forever.

00:17:23.293 --> 00:17:25.170
I'm willing to take that risk.

00:17:31.927 --> 00:17:35.180
Hey, pookums, contrary to what
I was sayin' earlier,

00:17:35.305 --> 00:17:38.141
melding minds with you
would be extremely bearable.

00:17:38.267 --> 00:17:40.143
You really mean it?

00:17:40.227 --> 00:17:41.895
Uh, yes.

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:47.317
Whoa-oh!

00:17:57.327 --> 00:17:59.162
Huh? Hey!

00:17:59.288 --> 00:18:02.583
Tubes? You're older
than you said you were.

00:18:02.708 --> 00:18:05.669
Come closer, Bender.
Let's become one.

00:18:05.752 --> 00:18:09.548
I prefer two. That way, we can still
be a horse for Halloween.

00:18:22.060 --> 00:18:24.146
Okay. Bender has her distracted.

00:18:24.271 --> 00:18:28.358
Now I can shut down her brain by
deactivating the carbonated logic matrix.

00:18:32.196 --> 00:18:36.325
Oh! I can't concentrate
with this obnoxious candy in my face.

00:18:36.450 --> 00:18:39.620
I'm on it. And maybe I'll
find those magic words while I'm at it.

00:18:39.745 --> 00:18:41.788
- Fat chance.
- Eh, no.

00:18:41.914 --> 00:18:43.790
Blecch!

00:18:43.916 --> 00:18:46.668
Ick!

00:18:46.793 --> 00:18:48.670
Oh. How about this one?

00:18:48.795 --> 00:18:54.259
Give it up, Fry. I've got to pop these
tops in a precise order.

00:18:56.220 --> 00:19:00.182
Halfway there. The ship should be getting
a bit less rational now.

00:19:00.307 --> 00:19:03.352
Me... want...
engulf... Bender!

00:19:07.356 --> 00:19:08.857
Only a few more.

00:19:10.234 --> 00:19:13.153
Hey! I won free admission
to Six Flags!

00:19:13.237 --> 00:19:15.614
Just one more reason
we must survive this.

00:19:20.244 --> 00:19:21.495
Um, Leela?

00:19:21.578 --> 00:19:25.040
Fry! I'll read your candy later...
when we're not dead.

00:19:30.212 --> 00:19:32.464
- What was that?
- Oh, nothing!

00:19:36.051 --> 00:19:40.806
We're gonna love
being each other, you sexy ion!

00:19:44.226 --> 00:19:46.812
Last one.

00:19:48.647 --> 00:19:50.858
Oh!

00:19:54.444 --> 00:19:56.280
It worked!

00:19:56.405 --> 00:19:58.907
Gravity normal.
Air returning.

00:19:59.032 --> 00:20:01.702
Terror replaced
by cautious optimism.

00:20:01.827 --> 00:20:03.829
We did it, Fry!

00:20:03.954 --> 00:20:05.831
Fry?

00:20:10.669 --> 00:20:13.755
You gave me your oxygen?
Oh, no!

00:20:13.881 --> 00:20:15.924
Breathe, Fry! Breathe!

00:20:27.311 --> 00:20:29.646
"U leave me breathless"?

00:20:31.565 --> 00:20:34.193
Happy Valentine's Day, Fry.

00:20:34.318 --> 00:20:37.070
Happy Valentine's Day.

00:20:38.989 --> 00:20:41.200
Bender, are you okay?

00:20:41.325 --> 00:20:43.869
What crazy thing
am I gonna date next?

00:20:43.994 --> 00:20:45.871
Well, at least it sounds
like you were able

00:20:45.996 --> 00:20:48.207
to keep your consciousness
separate from hers.

00:20:48.332 --> 00:20:52.753
Of course! Bender is a lone wolf,
a solitary eagle...

00:20:52.878 --> 00:20:54.963
A cuddly baby tapir.

00:20:55.088 --> 00:20:57.382
And that's why I love him.

00:20:58.759 --> 00:21:01.345
Well, I guess we better clean up
these millions of hearts.

00:21:01.470 --> 00:21:04.181
Nah. I've got
a lazier idea.

00:21:12.356 --> 00:21:16.235
As the candy hearts
poured into the fiery quasar,

00:21:16.360 --> 00:21:18.904
a wondrous thing happened,
why not?

00:21:19.029 --> 00:21:21.823
They vaporized
into a mystical love radiation

00:21:21.907 --> 00:21:23.909
that spread across the universe,

00:21:24.034 --> 00:21:26.745
destroying many, many planets,

00:21:26.870 --> 00:21:29.581
including two gangster planets
and a cowboy world.

00:21:29.706 --> 00:21:34.711
But one planet was exactly the right
distance to see the romantic rays...

00:21:34.837 --> 00:21:38.966
but not be destroyed
by them... Earth.

00:21:39.091 --> 00:21:43.178
So all over the world,
couples stood together in joy.

00:21:43.303 --> 00:21:45.180
And me, Zoidberg.

00:21:45.305 --> 00:21:50.853
And no one could have been happier unless
it wouldhave also been Valentine's Day.

00:21:50.936 --> 00:21:54.690
What? It was? Hooray!